On Nov 18, 8:48 am, juho.pohjalai...@gmail.com wrote:
> That is to say, if I have a +5 gauntlets of power, and I'd for
> some reason like to beat someone to death with them, would
> that +5 carry with it as a damage/hitting bonus?

When you mean "beat someone to death with them", do you mean
wielding them to hit the monster, or wearing them.  In either
case, I don't think that +5 has any effect: when wielded, I
think the damage depends only on their weight; when worn, you're
fighting bare handed, so damage depends on your skill in bare
handed or martial arts, plus various odds and ends.  Including
strength; you get a +3 damage bonus for strength 25, which
you'll always have when wearing them.

> I'm asking because, after my Stormbringer turned out to be
> compeletely useless against shades, a +3 shield of reflection
> proved to be an exceptionally capable weapon, even with the
> silver damage.

That's mainly because of the silver.  And IINM, a +0, or even a
-5 shield would have had the same effect.  (Shades practically
require silver, although I think I once got them with just
Excalibur.)

